{
  "normalizerVersion": 1,
  "description": "Golden vectors for the NG-word text normaliser. The server (firebase/functions/src/ngwords/normalize.ts) and the app offline filter (Dart port) MUST produce exactly `match` = normalizeForMatch(input) and `pattern` = normalizeForPatterns(input) for every vector. Dart has no built-in NFKC: use a Unicode normalisation package (e.g. unorm_dart) for step 1.",
  "algorithm": {
    "normalizeForMatch": [
      "1. Unicode NFKC",
      "2. lower-case",
      "3. katakana U+30A1..U+30F6 -> hiragana (code point - 0x60); ヷヸヹヺ (U+30F7..U+30FA) -> わゐゑを",
      "4. small kana -> full size: ぁぃぅぇぉっゃゅょゎゕゖ -> あいうえおつやゆよわかけ",
      "5. leetspeak, only inside maximal runs of [a-z0-9@$!] that contain at least one a-z letter: 0->o 1->i 3->e 4->a 5->s 7->t 8->b @->a $->s !->i",
      "6. strip every character except a-z, 0-9, hiragana U+3041..U+3096, 々 U+3005, CJK ideographs (U+3400..U+4DBF, U+4E00..U+9FFF, U+F900..U+FAFF, U+20000..U+3134F)",
      "7. collapse runs of the same character into one character"
    ],
    "normalizeForPatterns": [
      "1. Unicode NFKC",
      "2. lower-case",
      "3. kanji numerals 〇零一二三四五六七八九 -> 0-9",
      "4. remove whitespace and the separators - ‐ ‑ ‒ – — ― − ー － ~ 〜 ( ) （ ） [ ] 【 】 「 」 ・ _ / |"
    ],
    "matching": [
      "ng_words.json entries are normalised with normalizeForMatch at load time",
      "patterns are tested (unanchored unless the regex says otherwise) against normalizeForPatterns(text)",
      "then: if normalizeForMatch(text) is in allowExact -> clean; equals an exact entry -> blocked; contains a substring entry -> blocked"
    ]
  },
